1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,168
How do you stop a website taking more money than it is allowed?

2
00:00:03,218 --> 00:00:08,208
A concert hall can never sell its last seat twice, even with two clerks at the counter.

3
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:13,968
A website's payment limits work the same way: the most it may take per payment, and the most per day.

4
00:00:14,018 --> 00:00:18,144
A payment over the per-payment limit is refused the moment it is created.

5
00:00:18,194 --> 00:00:22,080
The daily limit is harder, because five buyers can pay at once.

6
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:27,888
So each charge reserves its amount on the day in one step, and only if the total still fits.

7
00:00:27,938 --> 00:00:30,192
Racing charges wait their turn.

8
00:00:30,242 --> 00:00:34,080
A charge that does not fit fails before any money moves.

9
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:40,200
And in front of it all, the edge accepts only modern encrypted connections and modest request sizes.

10
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:44,064
Next: how the system is installed, starting with its keys.
